{"step_index":446,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-09T15:25:16Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-09T19:25:16+04:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-09T19:25:16+04:00\nFile Path: `file:///home/koby/.gemini/config/AGENTS.md`\nTotal Lines: 61\nTotal Bytes: 2960\nShowing lines 1 to 61\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: # Global Rules & Memory — Antigravity\n2: \n3: ## Server Onboarding to IaC & Semaphore (Standard Operating Procedure)\n4: \n5: This workflow is permanently recorded for onboarding any new or legacy server into `infra-management-system` and Semaphore.\n6: \n7: ### 1. Zone & Network Reality (Hard Rule)\n8: * **Never mix network zones**: Inter-VLAN corporate firewalls strictly isolate DEV runners from PROD subnets.\n9: * Hosts with PROD naming (`*p-*`) or on PROD subnets (e.g. `172.30.39.0/24`, `172.30.230-231.0/24`) **must** be placed in `inventories/prod/hosts.yml`.\n10: * **Runner routing**:\n11:   - `dev` -> `th2-ansid-run1` (DEV VLANs `172.30.242-243.0/24`)\n12:   - `PROD` -> `th2-ansip-run1` (`172.30.199.225`, routes to datacenter & Martinique PROD)\n13: \n14: ### 2. Runner SSH Key & Host Setup (`spui-runner`)\n15: * **SSH Port**: `30`\n16: * **Account**: `spui-runner`, group `SSH_Users` (in `/etc/ssh/sshd_config` AllowGroups).\n17: * **Sudoers**: `/etc/sudoers.d/spui-runner` with `spui-runner ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD:ALL`.\n18: * **Authorized Keys** in `/etc/ssh/authorized_keys/spui-runner`:\n19:   - **PROD**: `ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIFW7ywu9PSVguYkbxDRMkU8FH/Ws09CDTWUSylusKkDA semaphore-runner-prod`\n20:   - **DEV / VAL**: `ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIFXxaA6I6XHKt1N9KMolZQQ7abBDA3r+RDl3iFc3l/Jo semaphore-runner`\n21: * **Manual bootstrap script**: `playbooks/bootstrap-spui-runner-manual.sh <zone>`.\n22: * **Warning**: Never close the active root/superuser session before verifying `spui-runner` login due to `AllowGroups`.\n23: \n24: ### 3. Inventory Declaration Pattern\n25: * In `inventories/<env>/hosts.yml`:\n26:   ```yaml\n27:   all:\n28:     hosts:\n29:       <hostname>:\n30:         ansible_host: <ip>\n31:         ansible_port: 30\n32:         ansible_user: spui-runner\n33:     children:\n34:       <dedicated_group>:\n35:         hosts:\n36:           <hostname>:\n37:   ```\n38: * **Isolation**: Keep new hosts OUT of shared application groups (`frontaux`, `backends`, `databases`) unless explicitly requested.\n39: * **Validate locally**:\n40:   ```bash\n41:   ansible-inventory -i inventories/<env>/hosts.yml --graph\n42:   ansible-inventory -i inventories/<env>/hosts.yml --host <hostname>\n43:   ```\n44: \n45: ### 4. Git & Automated Merge Request\n46: * 1 subject = 1 branch = 1 MR.\n47: * Automatically publish and create the MR in one shot via GitLab push options:\n48:   ```bash\n49:   git checkout -b feat/onboard-<hostname>-<env>\n50:   git add inventories/<env>/hosts.yml\n51:   git commit -m \"feat(inventory): add <hostname> to <env> inventory\"\n52:   git push -u -o merge_request.create -o merge_request.target=main -o merge_request.title=\"feat(inventory): add <hostname> to <env> inventory\" origin feat/onboard-<hostname>-<env>\n53:   ```\n54: \n55: ### 5. Semaphore Verification\n56: * Once merged, Semaphore's inventory follows `main`.\n57: * Execute read-only fact gathering via `playbooks/check-distro-kernel.yml` with `--limit <hostname>`:\n58:   - PROD: Template ID `131` (*Check Linux Distro and Kernel - PROD (recon)*)\n59:   - DEV: Template ID `130` (*Check Linux Distro and Kernel - DEV*)\n60: * Verify status reports `ONLINE` with accurate OS and kernel details.\n61: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
