{"step_index":451,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-09T15:25:29Z","thinking":"**Envisioning SSH automation enhancement**\n\nLeveraging the `$PATH` variable, a custom `kssh` script within `.local/bin` can significantly streamline SSH connection lookups. This script will query a structured inventory to resolve a hostname like `mtq-mailsrvp-01` to its IP address, port, and user credentials. The inventory lookup will be fast. This approach will automate the manual SSH process, saving time and potential errors.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"cat << 'EOF' > /home/koby/.ansible/scripts/kssh\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# ==============================================================================\n# Script: kssh (KeePass Server Pool Auto-SSH)\n# Purpose: Instant automated SSH to any server in the KeePass pool by\n#          hostname, IP, or keyword. Handles port, user, key, and password automatically.\n# ==============================================================================\n\nset -eo pipefail\n\nPOOL_JSON=\"${HOME}/.ansible/inventory/server_pool.json\"\n\nif [ ! -f \"$POOL_JSON\" ]; then\n    echo -e \"\\033[0;31m[ERROR] Server pool not found at ${POOL_JSON}.\\033[0m\"\n    echo -e \"Run: ansible-playbook ~/.ansible/playbooks/kdbx-pool.yml -e 'action=sync' to build it.\"\n    exit 1\nfi\n\nif [ -z \"$1\" ]; then\n    echo -e \"\\033[1mUsage:\\033[0m kssh <SERVER_NAME_OR_IP> [SSH_OPTIONS / COMMAND]\"\n    echo -e \"Example: kssh mtq-mailsrvp-01\"\n    echo -e \"         kssh trp-wextp-fe1 uptime\"\n    exit 1\nfi\n\nQUERY=\"$1\"\nshift || true\nEXTRA_ARGS=(\"$@\")\n\n# Query pool via python\nMATCHES_JSON=$(python3 -c \"\nimport json, sys\n\nquery = '''$QUERY'''.lower().strip()\nwith open('$POOL_JSON', 'r') as f:\n    data = json.load(f)\n\nservers = data.get('servers', [])\nresults = []\nfor s in servers:\n    haystack = ' '.join([\n        s.get('title', ''),\n        s.get('group', ''),\n        ' '.join(s.get('ips', [])),\n        s.get('username', ''),\n        s.get('notes', '')\n    ]).lower()\n    if query in haystack:\n        results.append(s)\n\n# Prioritize exact title match or non-recycle bin matches\nexact = [s for s in results if s.get('title', '').lower() == query]\nif exact:\n    # Filter out Recycle Bin if active match exists\n    active = [s for s in exact if 'recycle bin' not in s.get('group', '').lower()]\n    results = active if active else exact\nelse:\n    active = [s for s in results if 'recycle bin' not in s.get('group', '').lower()]\n    if active:\n        results = active\n\nprint(json.dumps(results))\n\")\n\nCOUNT=$(python3 -c \"import json; print(len(json.loads('''$MATCHES_JSON''')))\")\n\nif [ \"$COUNT\" -eq 0 ]; then\n    echo -e \"\\033[0;33m[WARN] No server found in KeePass pool matching '$QUERY'.\\033[0m\"\n    exit 1\nfi\n\nINDEX=0\nif [ \"$COUNT\" -gt 1 ]; then\n    echo -e \"\\033[1mMultiple matches found for '$QUERY':\\033[0m\"\n    python3 -c \"\nimport json\nmatches = json.loads('''$MATCHES_JSON''')\nfor i, m in enumerate(matches):\n    ip = m.get('primary_ip') or 'No IP'\n    port = f\\\":{m.get('port')}\\\" if m.get('port') else ''\n    print(f\\\"  [{i+1}] {m.get('title')} ({ip}{port}) - User: {m.get('username')} [{m.get('group')}]\\\")\n\"\n    read -p \"Select server [1-$COUNT]: \" CHOICE\n    INDEX=$((CHOICE - 1))\n    if [ \"$INDEX\" -lt 0 ] || [ \"$INDEX\" -ge \"$COUNT\" ]; then\n        echo \"Invalid selection.\"\n        exit 1\n    fi\nfi\n\n# Extract connection parameters\nTARGET_INFO=$(python3 -c \"\nimport json\nmatches = json.loads('''$MATCHES_JSON''')\nm = matches[$INDEX]\nprint(json.dumps({\n    'title': m.get('title', ''),\n    'ip': m.get('primary_ip', ''),\n    'port': m.get('port') or 22,\n    'user': m.get('username') or 'superuser',\n    'pass': m.get('password') or ''\n}))\n\")\n\nTITLE=$(python3 -c \"import json; print(json.loads('''$TARGET_INFO''')['title'])\")\nIP=$(python3 -c \"import json; print(json.loads('''$TARGET_INFO''')['ip'])\")\nPORT=$(python3 -c \"import json; print(json.loads('''$TARGET_INFO''')['port'])\")\nUSER=$(python3 -c \"import json; print(json.loads('''$TARGET_INFO''')['user'])\")\nPASS=$(python3 -c \"import json; print(json.loads('''$TARGET_INFO''')['pass'])\")\n\nif [ -z \"$IP\" ]; then\n    echo -e \"\\033[0;31m[ERROR] No IP address associated with '$TITLE'.\\033[0m\"\n    exit 1\nfi\n\necho -e \"\\033[0;32m[kssh]\\033[0m Connecting to \\033[1m${TITLE}\\033[0m (\\033[0;33m${USER}@${IP}:${PORT}\\033[0m)...\"\n\n# 1. First test if passwordless key authentication works for koby-bowser-ansible\nif ssh -o BatchMode=yes -o ConnectTimeout=2 -o StrictHostKeyChecking=accept-new -p \"$PORT\" -i \"${HOME}/.ssh/id_ed25519\" \"koby-bowser-ansible@${IP}\" \"true\" 2>/dev/null; then\n    exec ssh -p \"$PORT\" -i \"${HOME}/.ssh/id_ed25519\" \"koby-bowser-ansible@${IP}\" \"${EXTRA_ARGS[@]}\"\nfi\n\n# 2. Test if passwordless key authentication works for the designated user\nif ssh -o BatchMode=yes -o ConnectTimeout=2 -o StrictHostKeyChecking=accept-new -p \"$PORT\" -i \"${HOME}/.ssh/id_ed25519\" \"${USER}@${IP}\" \"true\" 2>/dev/null; then\n    exec ssh -p \"$PORT\" -i \"${HOME}/.ssh/id_ed25519\" \"${USER}@${IP}\" \"${EXTRA_ARGS[@]}\"\nfi\n\n# 3. If key auth not configured and password is available in pool, connect via sshpass\nif [ -n \"$PASS\" ] && command -v sshpass >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n    exec sshpass -p \"$PASS\" ssh -p \"$PORT\" -o StrictHostKeyChecking=accept-new \"${USER}@${IP}\" \"${EXTRA_ARGS[@]}\"\nfi\n\n# 4. Fallback to standard interactive SSH\nexec ssh -p \"$PORT\" -o StrictHostKeyChecking=accept-new \"${USER}@${IP}\" \"${EXTRA_ARGS[@]}\"\nEOF\nchmod +x /home/koby/.ansible/scripts/kssh\nln -sf /home/koby/.ansible/scripts/kssh /home/koby/.local/bin/kssh\n","Cwd":"/home/koby","WaitMsBeforeAsync":3000,"toolAction":"Running command","toolSummary":"Create kssh auto-SSH tool"}}]}
