{"step_index":498,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-09T15:28:34Z","content":"The automated SSH setup is now active and ready.\n\n### How the Setup Works\n\n#### 1. For You in the Terminal: `kssh`\nI installed a dedicated tool called **`kssh`** into your `$PATH` ([~/.local/bin/kssh](file:///home/koby/.local/bin/kssh)). \n\nWhenever you want to connect to any server, just type its name:\n```bash\nkssh trp-wextp-fe1\n```\n*(Or by IP: `kssh 172.30.230.97`, or by service name: `kssh mtq-mailsrvp-01`)*\n\n**What `kssh` does completely behind the scenes:**\n1. **Queries the KeePass Pool**: Instantly resolves the IP (`172.30.230.97`), Port (`30`), and username.\n2. **Excludes Stale Entries**: Prioritizes active servers over `Recycle Bin` duplicates.\n3. **Smart Authentication**:\n   - Checks if your local Ed25519 key ([~/.ssh/id_ed25519](file:///home/koby/.ssh/id_ed25519)) works (via `koby-bowser-ansible` or `superuser`).\n   - If key auth is not yet deployed, it automatically feeds the KeePass database password into `sshpass` so you log in without typing a single character!\n4. **Interactive vs Non-Interactive**:\n   - If you run `kssh <server>` with no command, it drops you into an interactive SSH session (and prompts a numbered menu if multiple accounts like `superuser` vs `root` exist).\n   - If you specify a user: `kssh -u root trp-wextp-fe1` or `kssh -u superuser trp-wextp-fe1`.\n\n---\n\n#### 2. For Me (Antigravity Assistant)\nThis workflow is permanently configured:\n- Whenever you tell me **\"ssh to `<server>`\"**, **\"check `<server>`\"**, or **\"run `<command>` on `<server>`\"**:\n- I will automatically execute `kssh <server> <command>` without asking you for the IP, port, user, or password.\n\n---\n\n### Live Verification Test\n\nI verified this live against `trp-wextp-fe1`:\n\n```bash\nkssh trp-wextp-fe1 uptime\n```\n\n**Result**:\n```text\n[kssh] Non-interactive mode: auto-selected trp-wextp-fe1 (superuser)\n[kssh